             {:prefix :site :path "openvino_telemetry/backend/backend_ga4.py" :lines [18 22]}]
   :problem "Selected server-route inspection is correctly not called an air gap, but the planning handoff still delegates the entire dependency/runtime-policy assessment. Installed OpenVINO 2025.4.1 imports its optional conversion tools, whose available path initializes telemetry with enable_opt_in_dialog=False and sends general_import. Installed telemetry accepts NO_FILE in that mode, and its GA4 backend has outbound urlopen/subprocess code. Thus 'local files plus no application forwarding' is not the complete available assessment."
   :impact "A real outbound opportunity exists in the dependency surface. This review observes DISK SOURCE only: it does NOT prove the optional import succeeded in the pinned worker, telemetry was enabled, any traffic occurred, or image/text bytes were forwarded. The import event is a startup path, not evidence that each OCR request resends it."
   :minimal-fix "Incorporate this bounded source assessment and explicitly dispose of current runtime/dependency configuration and the fixed batch's reachable path. Obtain narrowly scoped owner evidence for existing-worker telemetry/offline configuration or other concrete no-second-hop policy already in force, without secrets/native imports/restart. A newly edited environment or opt-out file alone is not proof of an already initialized singleton's state. If only application-level no-image-forwarding can be qualified, label exactly that and settle its sufficiency under the recorded consent; do not call it total egress denial. IF OS-enforced server egress denial is actually required, name the owner deployment prerequisite separately and HOLD: this plan grants no firewall, service hardening, namespace or restart operation. Do not invent a GovOne OCR call to authorize telemetry."
   :verification "The revised plan cites actual dependency/configuration evidence and a scoped judgment, rather than an unperformed assessment or an air-gap claim. Unsupported cloud/disclosure remains denied."}

  {:id :s7a-hard-plan/expiry-executor-and-registration-unbound
   :priority :P2 :context :己 :confidence 0.98
   :title "The raw-store expiry contract names no actual owner executor or registration seam."
   :anchors [{:path :plan :lines [141 149]}
             {:path :plan :lines [183 189]}
             {:prefix :coordinator :path "docs/notes/oikos-execution-plan.md" :lines [618 626]}
             {:prefix :product :path "eval/ocr-runner/README.md" :lines [156 170]}]
   :problem "'Qualify the existing owner's retention/cleanup executor' is a correct hold, but no executor, callable entry point, custody owner or durable registration acknowledgement is identified. The fixture matrix therefore has no concrete retention integration target. This reviewer found no such implementation in the inspected S7A checkout; that bounded search is not proof of host-wide absence."
   :impact "A 30-second process cannot perform its own future deletion, so expiry timestamps alone cannot complete this store's planning contract. Leaving the executor anonymous invites a new daemon or an unrelated service change outside the grant."
   :minimal-fix "Name the actual existing owner cleanup executor and narrowly scoped registration mechanism, including run-directory identity, 24h image/base64-request expiry, 7d OCR/text expiry, interrupted/orphan coverage and derived deletion. Specify which owner retains responsibility after client death and what registration evidence must exist BEFORE raw run data is admitted. If no executor is available, record that exact owner capability gap and keep durable-store/live admission held; do not invent a service or claim future deletion. Frozen versioned synthetic source fixtures are NOT expiry targets, and no automatic backup may extend the raw run copies' retention."
   :verification "Use owned synthetic run-directory records to verify registration failure blocks admission and the named executor targets only the registered run objects. Executor existence/registration remains unqualified here."}]

